ly inoperative — all historical successful runs pass the gate; (2) DISPATCH-NOTE AC requires an absolute-path normalisation test for --restore pre-state.json that is absent from the test suite; (3) GET→PUT transform test assertion omits (has(\\\\\\\"required_signatures\\\\\\\") | not), leaving the strip unverified against regression. Two MIN: (4) enforcement_level and contexts_url not stripped from PUT body — latent break-glass failure if GitHub's API rejects unknown nested fields; (5) workflow spec says paths-ignore for branch-protection-log+STATUS.md but implementation uses paths:, causing spurious workflow invocations. One nit: missing file-existence guard on RESTORE_PRE_STATE before cat. 0 CRIT, 3 MAJ, 2 MIN, 1 nit — not at fixpoint.\\\",\\n  \\\"carry_forward_verification\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-CORR-001\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED-IN-024B-CORE\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"cascade-status regex in check-invocation-log-entry.sh uses ([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]+?)\\\\\\\\s*$ — single-pass, trailing-prose-safe. Confirmed not regressed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-CORR-002\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"prior_restore_evidence_present is called only inside check_forward_mode_safety, which is guarded by if [ \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_MODE\\\\\\\" -eq 0 ] at line 518. No spurious contradiction message in restore mode.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-CORR-003\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED-IN-024B-CORE\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"TF-ticket match parameterises over canonicalized slug matching plan-doc invariant 2 literal regex. Not in scope for this slice.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"BOOTSTRAP-R7\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"CLOSED\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"Workflow paths: 024[C-Z]*/** excludes 024[AB]* from triggering. Job body case statement lists 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G as enforce=false tooling slices.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"workflow-runs API date filter embeds > in the URL query-param key name, not as a comparison value. The 60-day window is inoperative.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh line 478: gh api \\\\\\\"...&created>=${created_since}\\\\\\\". HTTP query-string parsing splits on first =; key becomes created>, value becomes the bare DATE string. GitHub receives an unrecognised param and ignores it, returning all successful runs. fake-gh test handler at line 262 checks for branch= but not the malformed created> key.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"forward-mode safety check degrades from 'successful run in last 60 days' to 'any historical successful run'. A repo with a single stale policy-check run from any time in the past passes the gate. The error message 'no successful workflow runs found... in the last 60 days' can never be triggered for repos with any prior history.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Change the URL fragment to &created%3E%3D${created_since} (percent-encoded) so the key is created and the value is >=DATE. Add a fake-gh assertion that the endpoint does NOT contain created> (> in key position) and DOES respond correctly to properly-formed created= queries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE AC lists 'absolute path normalisation' as a required --restore test case; no such test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"grep -E 'absolute|path.norm|readlink|realpath|RESTORE_PRE_STATE' across the test file returns no matches. All run_restore_case invocations hardcode --restore pre-state.json (relative path). The DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly lists 'absolute path normalisation' in the AC Tests: line for --restore mode tests.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The claim that --restore handles absolute paths is unverified. A future refactoring that breaks absolute-path reading (e.g. path normalization added without absolute-path handling) would go undetected. The AC is not satisfied.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test that writes the pre-state JSON to a temp file via an absolute path (e.g. ${TMPDIR}/abs-pre-state.json), passes --restore /abs/path/pre-state.json to run_restore_case, and asserts exit 0 with 'verification passed'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"GET→PUT transform test at line 1750 asserts _links, url, checks absent and enforce_admins boolean, but omits (has(\\\\\\\"required_signatures\\\\\\\") | not). The strip is implemented correctly but the test does not verify it.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Test fixture at line 1698 includes \\\\\\\"required_signatures\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"enabled\\\\\\\": true} at top level. Transform strip set at line 363 includes required_signatures. jq assertion at lines 1750-1761 checks has(\\\\\\\"_links\\\\\\\")|not, has(\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\")|not, has(\\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\")|not, enforce_admins==true, required_status_checks checks, but no required_signatures assertion. DISPATCH-NOTE AC item: 'GET→PUT transform' implicitly requires verifying all stripped fields.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If required_signatures is accidentally removed from the strip set, the PUT body would include it. GitHub's branch-protection PUT endpoint treats required_signatures as a separate sub-resource; including it in the PUT body would at best be silently ignored and at worst cause an API error during a live break-glass restore. The regression would not be caught by the test suite.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add and (has(\\\\\\\"required_signatures\\\\\\\") | not) to the jq assertion at line 1761. Also add (. .required_status_checks | has(\\\\\\\"_links\\\\\\\") | not) to cover the nested _links strip.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R4\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"transform strips only {_links, url, checks, required_signatures} but GitHub's real branch-protection GET response includes enforcement_level and contexts_url inside required_status_checks. These survive into the PUT body.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json strip condition at line 363: key in {\\\\\\\"_links\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"checks\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"required_signatures\\\\\\\"}. GitHub's GET /branches/BRANCH/protection returns required_status_checks.enforcement_level, required_status_checks.contexts_url, and required_status_checks.strict_required_status_checks_policy. Test fixture at line 1699 only includes _links and checks inside required_status_checks, not enforcement_level or contexts_url.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"On a real-world restore from a live captured pre-state.json, unknown nested fields in the PUT body may cause GitHub to return HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity, resulting in APPLY_FAIL=1. During a time-critical break-glass recovery the operator would see 'ERROR: unified PUT failed' and need to diagnose and manually strip additional fields.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Extend the strip set to also skip enforcement_level, contexts_url, strict_required_status_checks_policy. Add these fields to the test fixture and assert they are absent from put-body.json.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R5\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow trigger uses paths: for branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md, but DISPATCH-NOTE and D-047 specify paths-ignore: for those files, making the spec inconsistent with the implementation.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 18-21 list branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md under paths:, not paths-ignore:. DISPATCH-NOTE scope table says 'paths-ignore: [\\\\\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"STATUS.md\\\\\\\"]'. D-047 row repeats 'paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A PR that only touches branch-protection-log.md or STATUS.md (e.g. a standalone log-commit PR) triggers a workflow invocation that exits immediately with enforce=false via the no-dispatch-note short-circuit. Functionally equivalent to not triggering, but produces noise in PR check history and consumes CI quota unnecessarily.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Accept current behavior as correct (paths: is simpler and functionally equivalent) and update the DISPATCH-NOTE and D-047 prose to say paths: rather than paths-ignore:. Alternatively, restructure with paths: 024[C-Z]*/** only and paths-ignore: 024[AB]*/** for the complementary exclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-R6\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"RESTORE_PRE_STATE path has no explicit file-existence guard; the first read (cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" at line 607) produces a generic shell error on a missing file.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Argument parsing at lines 220-224 checks only [ -z \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" ]. No [ -f \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" ] guard before the cat. The Python open() inside validate_restore_source_json would also produce a generic FileNotFoundError rather than a script-level diagnostic.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor usability degradation: an operator who miskeys the pre-state path sees 'cat: pre-sate.json: No such file or directory' from the shell rather than an actionable script-level message. Does not affect nominal path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add [ -f \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" ] || { echo \\\\\\\"error: --restore file not found: ${RESTORE_PRE_STATE}\\\\\\\" >&2; exit 2; } immediately after the RESTORE_PRE_STATE empty-check at line 224.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"ffcaaf6d-bb3f-4ebb-b367-7b39f613b84b\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.44772775,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":15,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":131877,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":923020,\"output_tokens\":44958,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":131877,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":3425,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":123667,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":15591,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":15591},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1753,\"outputTokens\":23,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001868,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":15,\"outputTokens\":44958,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":923020,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":131877,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.44585975,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"3e0cab50-0676-42ab-b1c0-2970d233f549\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
