{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":558554,\"duration_api_ms\":558974,\"num_turns\":26,\"result\":\"I now have all the information needed to produce the review. Let me compile the findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"R1-completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"All 8 DISPATCH-NOTE ACs map to concrete committed artefacts: --restore mode (enable-required-check.sh lines 600-716), forward-mode safety check (lines 459-505), --expected-wrapper-sha tag validation (lines 440-457), ADOPT-001 §12.8 3-gate break-glass playbook, CI workflow check-invocation-log-entry.yml, test coverage for all restore behaviours and forward-mode SHA validation (test file lines 1691-2742), D-047, and step-7 placeholder stub committed. Plan-doc invariant 2 (CI-enforced) is closed by the workflow wiring; invariant 7 (<30 min rollback SLO) is documented and the step-7 demo AC is correctly left unchecked at R1 with a proper tracking entry. All carry-forward R8 findings are addressed: R8-CORR-001/003 closed in 024B-core; R8-CORR-002 tight via restore-mode guard (lines 220-249); R8-SAFE-001 addressed via WARNING+CAUTION in §12.8+log block; R8-SAFE-002 via working-tree diff in prior_restore_evidence_present(); R8 bootstrap via paths+job-body short-circuit. VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper lists all four new flags. Plan-doc §6 024C gating correctly requires both 024B-core+extras+FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. Anti-descoping respected; SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md explicitly documents the split rationale. Two defects found: one MAJ (conflicting evidence file path between STATUS.md TF and DISPATCH-NOTE), one MIN (ADOPT-001 §12.8 SLO phrasing omits 'merge-restored' qualifier), one MIN (paths-ignore spec vs actual workflow implementation).\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 references the demo evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` (no PLACEHOLDER suffix), while the DISPATCH-NOTE AC (step-in-scope table, AC checklist) and the committed placeholder file both use `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md`. The two references conflict for the single merge-blocking AC closure path.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 310: `restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` (no PLACEHOLDER); DISPATCH-NOTE scope table row and AC checklist item 8: `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md`; placeholder file at that path instructs operator to 'Replace this file's content'. The TF entry and the placeholder/DISPATCH-NOTE disagree on which file the operator should update.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operator performing the step-7 demo has conflicting instructions: TF says commit to `restore-roundtrip-evidence.md`; placeholder file says replace its own content. If operator creates a new file matching the TF name, the AC (which references the PLACEHOLDER path) remains unchecked and the merge gate is ambiguous. Audit trail post-merge references an incorrect file path in STATUS.md.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update STATUS.md TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 parenthetical evidence path to `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` to match the DISPATCH-NOTE AC and the committed placeholder file. Alternatively, rename the placeholder file to `restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` and update DISPATCH-NOTE + placeholder accordingly, but the DISPATCH-NOTE path is more visible so STATUS.md is the cheaper fix.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1 states the rollback SLO as 'less than 30 minutes from operator decision to restored branch-protection state', omitting 'merge-restored' from plan-doc invariant 7's definition. The plan-doc explicitly includes the invocation-log entry commit in the 30-minute window; §12.8 covers only the API-level state change.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Plan-doc §2 invariant 7: '<30 minutes from operator decision to merge-restored state'. ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1 closing paragraph: 'less than 30 minutes from operator decision to restored branch-protection state.' The word 'merge-restored' (covering the log entry commit) is absent from §12.8.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A future operator reading only §12.8 may believe the SLO is satisfied once the API state is restored, without committing the invocation-log entry. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure per D-035 and is required for the audit trail to be complete.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Amend ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1 closing sentence to: 'The rollback SLO is less than 30 minutes from operator decision to merge-restored state (API state restored + invocation-log entry committed), per plan-doc invariant 7.'\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE specifies `paths-ignore: ['docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**', 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md', 'STATUS.md']` as a GitHub workflow trigger configuration, but the committed `check-invocation-log-entry.yml` uses only a `paths` (inclusive) trigger with no `paths-ignore` stanza. The spec description and the implementation differ in mechanism, creating a documentation inconsistency for future reviewers.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE scope table for workflow: 'paths-ignore: [...]' listed as a workflow config property. check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 13-20: only `paths:` block present, no `paths-ignore:`. The bootstrap defect is handled in the job body (lines 44-67 of the workflow) not via paths-ignore.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Future editors reading the DISPATCH-NOTE may expect a `paths-ignore` stanza in the workflow and incorrectly diagnose its absence as a bug. The functional outcome is equivalent (bootstrap protected via job-body short-circuit), so no runtime impact.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update DISPATCH-NOTE scope table description to accurately describe the actual mechanism: 'Bootstrap guard: job-body short-circuit exits 0 for tooling slices (024A/024B-core/024B-extras/024G) or PRs with no cascade DISPATCH-NOTE in diff; paths trigger excludes 024A/024B-* organically via 024[C-Z]* pattern.' Remove the misleading `paths-ignore` specification.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"b7bdf9e6-51a0-4be6-9286-fe0dd1c462b5\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.12774245,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":14,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":108979,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":874004,\"output_tokens\":30325,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":108979,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":9477,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":115624,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":736,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":736},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1823,\"outputTokens\":26,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0019529999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":14,\"outputTokens\":30325,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":874004,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":108979,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.12578945,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"32ab800c-3d8f-495b-b75a-35cba0a97fe5\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
